Okay, so after hacking away enough, I think I have come up with a
decent way to identify scrolls. If anyone has additional
techniques/tips, please let me know. I've tried to keep it short, so
there is some detail missing.

My newest way:

First, scrolls fall into 8 price "classes"; 0, 20, 50, 60, 80, 100,
200, 300. Of these classes, going to a shop, pricing the scrolls and
knowing the scroll appearance can identify every scroll in the 0, 20,
50 and 60 classes. This leaves the 80, 100, 200 and 300 classes.

I call the scrolls according to class (i.e. NR 9 called 80). I use
this information to identify the types of effects I can expect from a
certain class of spells. I determine the "holy status" (blessed etc.)
of each scroll, then choose a suitable location with suitable
conditions to read the scrolls (i.e. the 100 class contains fire,
which is a dumb class of scrolls to read near a priest or with a bunch
of papery things that burn in hand).  In all cases, I like to have a
monster free zone to do my testing.

If a scroll is cursed, I don't read it. Since the scroll I most want
to avoid reading is the amnesia scroll, I can use a blessed identify
scroll to id scrolls in the 200 class (the amnesia class). If it's
really early in the game, then I don't worry about reading an amnesia
scroll.

So, anyone have some additional techniques for safely identifying
scrolls?

